    "body": "# ZORR BLATT — UNIFIED ARCHIVE / GLOBAL CHAT ENTRYPOINT\n\nSTATUS = ACTIVE GLOBAL RESTORE ENTRYPOINT\nSINGLE_ENTRYPOINT = https://github.com/Lester-Sparx/zorr-blatt-shared-hq/issues/204\nAUTHORITY = current `main` + Permanent Archive V1 RAW history\nARCHIVE_BRANCH = `zb-archive-v1`\nARCHIVE_ROOT = `hq/archive-v1`\nFORMAT = plain Git + Markdown/JSON + SHA-256\nCUSTOM_MEMORY_SERVICE = NONE\n\n## ANY CHAT BOOTSTRAP\n\nWhen SPARX says `ZORR MODE`, restore from this issue instead of relying on chat/session memory.\n\n1. Open this issue (#204).\n2. Fresh-read current `main` HEAD.\n3. Fresh-read `ZORR_EXECUTION_CONSTITUTION.md` and `AGENTS.md` from that exact `main`.\n4. Fresh-read the exact active task/tracker/PR/workflow evidence named by the current request.\n5. For external HOME-PC / Babylon / ComfyUI / executor evidence, read the comments on this issue.\n6. For historical reconstruction, conflicts, or missing context, read the original event under branch `zb-archive-v1`, root `hq/archive-v1`.\n7. RAW/fresher GitHub evidence always outranks summaries and chat memory.\n8. If required evidence is missing or contradictory, return `DURABLE_CONTEXT_NOT_PROVEN`; never guess.\n\n## PUBLIC FALLBACK — NO CONNECTOR REQUIRED\n\nThis repository is public. A chat without the GitHub connector can restore through ordinary web access using this stable issue URL, then follow the public repository links above. Do not require SPARX to copy the archive into the chat.\n\n## HARD LAW\n\n`CHAT != ARCHIVE`\n`ONE PUBLIC ENTRYPOINT -> CURRENT MAIN / EXACT TASK / RAW ARCHIVE`\n`RAW ORIGINAL EVENT > VERIFIED GITHUB HISTORY > CURRENT TASK EVIDENCE > DERIVED SUMMARY > CHAT MEMORY`\n\nPermanent Archive V1 preserves GitHub issue/comment events byte-for-byte and content-addresses RAW evidence by SHA-256. Corrections append/supersede; archived RAW history is never rewritten.\n\n## EXTERNAL EVIDENCE FEED\n\nExternal terminal evidence is recorded as comments here with durable coordinates such as:\n\n- `SOURCE_REPO`\n- `SOURCE_HEAD`\n- `SOURCE_BRANCH`\n- `WORKFLOW_RUN_ID` / `JOB_ID`\n- `ARTIFACT_ID` / release tag\n- `FILE_NAME`\n- `SHA256`\n- `STATE = PASS | FAIL | BLOCKED | CANDIDATE`\n- `NEXT`\n\nNo prose-only PASS. No chat-only terminal state.\n\n## LARGE BINARY LAW\n\nDo not grow the repository with large binaries.\n\n`binary bytes -> immutable/versioned release asset`\n`metadata -> SHA-256-bound manifest / archive evidence`\n\nActions artifacts are transport/CI evidence and may expire; durable approved bytes must be referenced by immutable hash/version coordinates.\n\n## BOUNDARY\n\nThis issue is the single discovery/restore entrypoint, not a second source of truth. Current `main`, exact task evidence, and Permanent Archive V1 RAW history remain authoritative.\n\nNo new daemon, vector database, proprietary memory backend, or custom archive engine is required for this global entrypoint.",
